      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While accepting pain without fighting it can be a powerful coping strategy, giving up on finding relief or comfort only tends to amplify suffering rather than solve it. Many professionals focus on reducing the intensity of your pain and helping you live in the present moment, rather than demanding a complete \"fix\" to your identity. Exploring this perspective with a counselor who understands trauma might help you find a balance between accepting where you are and locating small moments of relief or acceptance.",
      "source": "target",
